        "content": "## MLOps Container Infrastructure\n\nComplete container and host observability: service probe status, per-container CPU/memory/network, PostgreSQL connection counts and database sizes, HTTP probe durations, and host system resources.\n\n### Key Panels\n| Panel | What to look for |\n|:------|:-----------------|\n| Status row (top) | All 6 green = full stack healthy. Any red = investigate immediately |\n| Container Memory (MiB) | Steady growth = memory leak. Sudden drop = container restart |\n| Container CPU (%) | Spike = processing load. Sustained high CPU = capacity issue |\n| PostgreSQL Active Connections | Steady baseline expected. Spike = connection leak |\n| HTTP Probe Duration | Should be <200ms. Rising probe duration = service degradation |\n\n**Data sources:** `probe_success`, `pg_up`, `container_memory_usage_bytes`, `container_cpu_usage_seconds_total`, `container_network_*`, `pg_stat_activity_count`, `probe_duration_seconds`, node_exporter metrics\n\n*Created: Session 10 \u2014 GF-NEW-1 (Sprint 4)*",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
